## D170 · 2026-10-25 · Phase close-out: what the code review removed, fixed and left

Alex: "我们跑一个code review 清理一下过程中stale code 和 bloat 然后准备写好文档push". Two read-only Codex reviews (product code with its tests; tooling), each finding checked against the code before acting (log row 50). The full measured state is commit `f4ff787`; everything removed here is there.
- Removed: the retired research harness `poc/hierarchy_study/` (17 experiments and 15 test files, D146–D162, none adopted; its tests wrote three SQLite files to the repository root through a module-named path, also removed); five finished one-off scripts (`jev_poc.py`, `supersedes_probe.py`, `succession_probe.py`, `key_views.py`, `review_keyed_run.py`; results in the build log and `poc/reports/`); six product functions with no caller (`judging.judge_one`, `matching.same_orientation`, `Universe.canonical_scope`, `testdb.days_with_items`, `store.lineage_of_view`, `store.replaced_by`) and six unused constants.
- Fixed: the preflight's matching section now judges Jev records (it had skipped all 250 of the Jev ledger) and fails when every record of a ledger is skipped; the cost reports read the one price table (`model.PRICES`) and refuse an unpriced model; the benchmark stops when its evidence scorer fails; Jev succession eligibility has one rule (`jev_matching.can_succeed`); a test no longer reads the real credentials file, another no longer writes the real service archive; the newsroom category rule has one owner that its test exercises; the replay requires the ledger and archive it writes and defaults to `poc-v23` and the current item window; the compose file uses the adopted idea configuration `poc-v9`.
- Left, with the reason: the dependency-cycle pass in `matching.check` (its refusal wording reaches stored retry requests, so merging it would change replayed requests); the two ladder validators (admission of a new ladder and reading of a stored one are different jobs); splitting `matching.check`, `writing._write` and `idea.read_idea` (behaviour-preserving refactors of the core without a measurement round); unused parameters and result fields (signature churn across many call sites); the corpus harvesters' shared fetch code; the test-only `search.fake_embed` in the search module; `scripts/review_english_run.py` counting equal model-written scopes as a breach (D155 makes them a lead, not identity). The reviewers' lead that the API's `poc-v9` default was stale was wrong: it is the adopted idea configuration (D135/D145).

## D171 · 2026-10-25 · Review and free proofs for the day-batch acceleration proposal

- Alex asked to review the extraction/Jev/per-day acceleration plan deeply and test it against the stored golds and result databases. Scope is review and isolated offline proofs; no product-contract change, runtime adoption or paid comparison follows automatically.
- The [review](research/2026-10-25-day-batch-review/review.md) and its scripts reconstruct 960/960 extraction requests from the two saved v23 ledgers. Day-start context differs for 214/480 Jev-arm requests and 168/480 control requests; rechecking the same raw answers with day-start IDs loses 73/797 and 62/744 evidence items. Extraction depends on earlier theses as well as groups. The Jev arm has 86/320 final repeat/replace decisions targeting same-day evidence, and Jev membership alone cannot declare the 26 new groups.
- At 32 workers, a three-wave schedule using recorded Jev call durations projects 8.6× on July 27 and 3.2× over 31 nonempty days, before reconciliation/rate-limit overhead. This replaces the unsupported general 10× claim, not the speed target. It is a schedule estimate, not fresh measured latency. Judging already uses six workers per dependency level.
- Recommendation awaiting Alex's choice: concurrent request preparation with exact read validation before sequential commits, retaining D149/D159 semantics; re-run requests whose inputs changed. A more aggressive day-start extraction contract must be decided and tested separately. The review defines both boundaries, failure/recovery states, local-ID namespacing, evaluation limits and staged tests.
- Verification: 128 product/corpus/diagnostic tests passed; two diagnostic mutants were caught; preflight judged 250 stored Jev records with no skipped records. Existing golds remain unchanged. No batching runtime or fresh model-quality pass is claimed.
- A read-only review independently reproduced the 960 request message pairs and schemas, the stale-reference losses and the timing projection; no serious finding against the proposed contract. Runtime implementation and live measurement remain the next, separate steps.

## D172 · 2026-10-25 · Build the isolated ordered-concurrency POC

- Alex accepted the D171 recommendation: “yes be super careful about the logic ... do not fuck up the order ... flag it immediately”. Implement concurrent preparation with current-prefix validation and one ordered writer. Keep the default serial path and its tests unchanged. Group ownership and thesis/evidence semantics do not move.
- Speculative calls may precede earlier commits in the experimental path; accepted handovers and writes may not. Stale prepared requests are recomputed; earlier failure cancels pending work and drains running calls without accepting later results. This scheduling distinction is explicit, not an accidental weakening of D159.
- The [first implementation slice](research/2026-10-25-day-batch-review/implementation.md) covers offline coordinator, independent Jev calls and failure/restart verification on temporary storage. No paid call, new spending cap or default activation is authorized by this slice. The current per-item spend check is not safe reservation accounting for concurrent paid calls; resolve it before a live comparison.
"""Extraction (docs/prd/05-extraction.md): the whole item goes to the model with the five-block prompt of its
category; the answer is evidence linked to the shown views or to this item's candidate views, and candidate views
written in full. Code checks the sources (the quote is in the text, every link points at a shown view or a
candidate), the ladders (five rungs or two) and the rule that quarterly numbers are evidence, not views.

Prompt versions 1–5 ask and answer in Chinese; version 6 and later ask and answer in English (D163). The schema,
the request text and the retry note follow the version; every answer is read in the canonical vocabulary."""
import dataclasses
import datetime
import json
import re

from . import config, model, vocabulary

TIERS = vocabulary.TIERS
LEGACY_TIERS = list(vocabulary.LEGACY['tier'])
LEGACY_KINDS = list(vocabulary.LEGACY['kind'])
MAX_TEXT_CHARS = 400_000
ENGLISH_FROM = 6                  # the first extraction prompt version written in English
GROUPS_FROM = 7                   # the first version whose candidates carry research-group membership (D149)
ALIASES_FROM = 9                  # the first version whose declared groups carry aliases, so code decides identity and membership (D166)


def version_number(version):
    return int(str(version or '').lstrip('v') or 0)


def is_english(version):
    return version_number(version) >= ENGLISH_FROM


def has_groups(version):
    return version_number(version) >= GROUPS_FROM


def base_schema(english):
    kinds = vocabulary.KINDS if english else LEGACY_KINDS
    tiers = TIERS if english else LEGACY_TIERS
    return {
        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence', 'candidates'],
        'properties': {
            'evidence': {'type': 'array', 'items': {
                'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,
                'required': ['id', 'quote', 'one_line', 'speaker', 'original_who', 'original_day', 'tier', 'event_time', 'links'],
                'properties': {
                    'id': {'type': 'string'}, 'quote': {'type': 'string'}, 'one_line': {'type': 'string'}, 'speaker': {'type': 'string'},
                    'original_who': {'type': 'string'}, 'original_day': {'type': 'string'}, 'tier': {'type': 'string', 'enum': tiers},
                    'event_time': {'type': 'string'}, 'links': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}}}},
            'candidates': {'type': 'array', 'items': {
                'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,
                'required': ['id', 'object', 'kind', 'looks_at', 'question', 'rungs', 'due_day', 'year', 'evidence_ids'],
                'properties': {
                    'id': {'type': 'string'}, 'object': {'type': 'string'}, 'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': kinds},
                    'looks_at': {'type': 'string'}, 'question': {'type': 'string'},
                    'rungs': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['label', 'condition'],
                                                           'properties': {'label': {'type': 'string'}, 'condition': {'type': 'string'}}}},
                    'due_day': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': r'^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$'},      # a date, enforced by the schema, not by prose
                    'year': {'type': 'string'}, 'evidence_ids': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}}}},
        },
    }


SCHEMA = base_schema(english=False)          # the shape of the answers stored under versions 1–3

# keyed-views-plan.md 2.1: the key a candidate carries from prompt version v4 on; the ladder's rungs carry numeric bounds
MEASURES = ['total_revenue', 'segment_revenue', 'product_revenue', 'gross_margin', 'operating_margin', 'operating_expense_growth', 'total_expenses', 'operating_loss',
            'tax_rate', 'capex', 'shipments_or_capacity', 'run_rate', 'design_wins', 'event', 'spend_total', 'financing_amount', 'price', 'capacity', 'growth_rate', 'policy_event', 'other']
EVENT_TYPES = ['launch', 'shipment', 'licence', 'approval', 'deal_close', 'deployment', 'other', 'n/a']
BASES = ['GAAP', 'non_GAAP', 'n/a']
UNITS = ['USD', 'percent', 'count', 'GW', 'MW', 'TWD', 'multiple', 'n/a']
# D167 (2026-10-25): from version 10 the vocabulary names a market's size and a project's cost as their own measures; the week filed an
# accelerator TAM and a data-center project's cost as spend_total, the aggregate of spending, which no identity rule could then tell apart
MEASURES_V10 = MEASURES[:MEASURES.index('spend_total') + 1] + ['market_size', 'project_cost'] + MEASURES[MEASURES.index('spend_total') + 1:]
MEASURES_V10_FROM = 10


def key_fields(measures=MEASURES):
    return {'measure': {'type': 'string', 'enum': list(measures)}, 'scope': {'type': 'string'},
            'period_start': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': r'^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$'}, 'period_end': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': r'^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$'},
            'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': BASES}, 'unit': {'type': 'string', 'enum': UNITS}, 'event_type': {'type': 'string', 'enum': EVENT_TYPES}}


BOUND = {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}]}


def keyed_schema(english=False, measures=MEASURES):
    """The base schema with the key fields on every candidate and numeric bounds on every rung."""
    schema = base_schema(english)
    candidate = schema['properties']['candidates']['items']
    fields = key_fields(measures)
    candidate['properties'].update(fields)
    candidate['required'] += list(fields)
    rung = candidate['properties']['rungs']['items']
    rung['properties'].update({'lo': BOUND, 'hi': BOUND})
    rung['required'] += ['lo', 'hi']
    return schema


LOCAL_GROUP = r'n[1-9][0-9]*'
# a company's own reported or guided lines: they belong to the company and never found a research group by themselves
FINANCIAL_LINES = {'total_revenue', 'segment_revenue', 'gross_margin', 'operating_margin', 'operating_expense_growth', 'total_expenses', 'operating_loss', 'tax_rate', 'capex', 'run_rate'}


def tracks_a_matter(candidate):
    """A candidate that can start a research group: a theme quantity, an event or policy event, a product or market figure;
    not a company's own financial line (which may join a group another thesis started, never found one)."""
    return candidate.get('kind') == 'theme' or candidate.get('measure') not in FINANCIAL_LINES


def grouped_schema(shown_group_ids, aliases=False, measures=MEASURES):
    """The English keyed schema plus research-group membership (D149, the D147 reference shape): each candidate cites one or
    more groups, each either a group id shown in this request or a local id declared in new_groups; the pattern is built
    from the shown ids, so an unseen group cannot be cited."""
    schema = keyed_schema(english=True, measures=measures)
    pattern = '^(?:' + LOCAL_GROUP + ''.join('|' + re.escape(g) for g in shown_group_ids) + ')$'
    candidate = schema['properties']['candidates']['items']
    candidate['properties']['group_refs'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': pattern}}
    candidate['required'].append('group_refs')
    group_fields = {'id': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': '^' + LOCAL_GROUP + '$'}, 'name': {'type': 'string'}, 'scope': {'type': 'string'}}
    if aliases:
        group_fields['aliases'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}
    schema['properties']['new_groups'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': list(group_fields), 'properties': group_fields}}
    schema['required'].append('new_groups')
    return schema


def schema_for(version, shown_group_ids=()):
    number = version_number(version)
    measures = MEASURES_V10 if number >= MEASURES_V10_FROM else MEASURES
    if number >= GROUPS_FROM:
        return grouped_schema(shown_group_ids, aliases=number >= ALIASES_FROM, measures=measures)
    if number >= ENGLISH_FROM:
        return keyed_schema(english=True)
    return keyed_schema() if number >= 4 else SCHEMA


@dataclasses.dataclass
class Handover:
    evidence: list
    candidates: list
    dropped: list
    call_id: int
    request_sha256: str
    cached: bool
    cost_usd: float
    return [r['view_id'] for r in conn.execute('select view_id from evidence_links where evidence_id=? order by id', (evidence_id,))]


def evidence_ids_under(conn, view_id):
    return [r['evidence_id'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))]


# ---------- processing record and pool ----------

def mark_step(conn, input_id, sequence_no, step, result, reason, publication_day, at):
    insert(conn, 'processing_steps', input_id=input_id, sequence_no=sequence_no, step=step, result=result, reason=reason, publication_day=publication_day, at=at)


def last_step(conn, input_id):
    row = conn.execute('select step, result, sequence_no from processing_steps where input_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (input_id,)).fetchone()
    return dict(row) if row else None


def is_processed(conn, input_id):
    return bool(conn.execute("select 1 from processing_steps where input_id=? and step='handed_over' and result='ok'", (input_id,)).fetchone())


def next_sequence(conn):
    row = conn.execute('select coalesce(max(sequence_no), 0) from processing_steps').fetchone()
    return int(row[0]) + 1


def pool(conn, kind, key, example, seq):
    insert(conn, 'review_pool_entries', kind=kind, key=key, example_json=json.dumps(example, ensure_ascii=False)[:4000], seq=seq)


def last_check(conn, view_id):
    """The last round that read this view: its item's publication day and id (the card's 上次核对 line)."""
    row = conn.execute('select input_id, publication_day from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()
    if row:
        return row['publication_day'], row['input_id']
    row = conn.execute('select s.publication_day, s.input_id from evidence_links l join evidence_sources s on s.evidence_id=l.evidence_id where l.view_id=? order by s.id desc limit 1', (view_id,)).fetchone()
    return (row['publication_day'], row['input_id']) if row else (None, None)


def complete_day(conn, day, seq, at):
    insert(conn, 'days_completed', day=day, seq=seq, at=at)


def last_completed_day(conn):
    row = conn.execute('select day from days_completed order by id desc limit 1').fetchone()
"""Config (docs/prd/03-config.md): a versioned file of the settings a person chooses, with a checksum written into
every model call's record. A version that references a missing setting is refused whole."""
import dataclasses
import hashlib
import json
import os

PROMPTS = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), 'prompts')


class ConfigError(ValueError):
    pass


def prompt_path(name):
    """The file of a prompt the config names, for example role-v1.txt or matching-v1.txt."""
    return os.path.join(PROMPTS, name)


def _prompt_files(extraction, matching, rejudging, idea=None):
    """03-config: a version that names a prompt that does not exist is refused whole. An extraction setting's
    prompt_version is '<category>-<v>': block 2 and 4 come from categories-<v>.json (the category's entry) and the
    role from role-<v>.txt; matching, re-judging and the idea reading name their file without the extension."""
    for category, setting in extraction.items():
        prefix, _, version = setting.prompt_version.rpartition('-')
        if prefix != category or not version:
            raise ConfigError(f'extraction.{category}: prompt_version {setting.prompt_version!r} must be {category}-<version>')
        categories_file = prompt_path(f'categories-{version}.json')
        if not os.path.exists(categories_file) or not os.path.exists(prompt_path(f'role-{version}.txt')):
            raise ConfigError(f'extraction.{category}: prompts for version {version!r} do not exist')
        with open(categories_file, encoding='utf-8') as handle:
            if category not in json.load(handle):
                raise ConfigError(f'extraction.{category}: categories-{version}.json has no entry for {category}')
    for setting in (matching, rejudging, idea):
        if setting is not None and not os.path.exists(prompt_path(setting.prompt_version + '.txt')):
            raise ConfigError(f'{setting.name}: prompt {setting.prompt_version}.txt does not exist')


@dataclasses.dataclass(frozen=True)
class Setting:
    name: str
    model: str
    prompt_version: str
    temperature: float
    reasoning_effort: str
    max_output_tokens: int
    engine: str = 'llm'       # matching only: 'llm' (the generative call) or 'jev' (TypeSafe Jev, views/jev_matching.py)


ENGINES = ('llm', 'jev')


@dataclasses.dataclass(frozen=True)
class Config:
    version: str
    checksum: str
    provider: str
    search_top_n: int
    extraction: dict          # category -> Setting
    matching: Setting
    rejudging: Setting
    final_verdict: Setting
    idea: Setting = None      # the service's reading of a user's idea (docs/poc/idea-card.md); absent in pipeline-only configs

    def extraction_setting(self, category):
        setting = self.extraction.get(category)
        if setting is None:
            raise ConfigError(f'no extraction setting for category {category} in config {self.version}')
        return setting


REQUIRED = ('model', 'prompt_version', 'temperature', 'reasoning_effort', 'max_output_tokens')


def _setting(name, raw):
    if not isinstance(raw, dict):
        raise ConfigError(f'setting {name} is missing')
    missing = [key for key in REQUIRED if key not in raw]
    if missing:
        raise ConfigError(f'setting {name} lacks {missing}')
    engine = str(raw.get('engine', 'llm'))
    if engine not in ENGINES:
        raise ConfigError(f'setting {name}: engine {engine!r} is not one of {ENGINES}')
    return Setting(name=name, model=str(raw['model']), prompt_version=str(raw['prompt_version']),
                   temperature=float(raw['temperature']), reasoning_effort=str(raw['reasoning_effort']),
                   max_output_tokens=int(raw['max_output_tokens']), engine=engine)


def load(path):
    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as handle:
        text = handle.read()
    raw = json.loads(text)
    for key in ('version', 'provider', 'search_top_n', 'extraction', 'matching', 'rejudging', 'final_verdict'):
        if key not in raw:
            raise ConfigError(f'config lacks {key}')
    canonical = json.dumps({k: v for k, v in raw.items() if not k.startswith('_')}, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)
    checksum = hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()[:16]
    extraction = {category: _setting(f'extraction.{category}', setting) for category, setting in raw['extraction'].items()}
    matching, rejudging = _setting('matching', raw['matching']), _setting('rejudging', raw['rejudging'])
    idea = _setting('idea', raw['idea']) if 'idea' in raw else None
    _prompt_files(extraction, matching, rejudging, idea)       # final_verdict is kept in the file but no POC step calls it
    return Config(version=str(raw['version']), checksum=checksum, provider=str(raw['provider']),
                  search_top_n=int(raw['search_top_n']), extraction=extraction,
                  matching=matching, rejudging=rejudging, final_verdict=_setting('final_verdict', raw['final_verdict']), idea=idea)
"""The research list (docs/prd/01-universe.md): which objects exist and which categories each is watched in. The
only place that decides what is processed. Loaded from poc/universe.json."""
import json
import re


class Universe:
    def __init__(self, raw):
        self.version = raw['version']
        self.companies = {c['id']: c for c in raw['companies']}
        self.themes = {t['id']: t for t in raw['themes']}
        self.theme_names = {t['name']: t['id'] for t in raw['themes']}
        self.theme_names.update({t['legacy_name']: t['id'] for t in raw['themes'] if t.get('legacy_name')})

    def has(self, object_id):
        return object_id in self.companies or object_id in self.themes

    def kind(self, object_id):
        if object_id in self.companies:
            return 'company'
        if object_id in self.themes:
            return 'theme'
        return None

    def resolve(self, text):
        """An object named by ticker, theme id, theme name, company name or one of the object's aliases (a theme's
        former name is an alias); None when not on the list."""
        if not text:
            return None
        key = text.strip()
        if key in self.companies or key in self.themes:
            return key
        if key in self.theme_names:
            return self.theme_names[key]
        upper = key.upper()
        if upper in self.companies:
            return upper
        for company in self.companies.values():
            if company['name'].lower() == key.lower():
                return company['id']
        for record in list(self.themes.values()) + list(self.companies.values()):
            if any(alias.casefold() == key.casefold() for alias in record.get('aliases') or []):
                return record['id']
        return None

    def watches(self, object_id, category):
        record = self.companies.get(object_id) or self.themes.get(object_id)
        return bool(record and category in record['categories'])

    def theme_list(self, legacy=False):
        """(id, name) per theme; legacy=True gives the name a Chinese prompt version printed (legacy_name, else name), so its stored requests replay byte-identical."""
        return [(t['id'], (t.get('legacy_name') or t['name']) if legacy else t['name']) for t in self.themes.values()]

    def watch_list(self, object_id):
        """The analyst's quantities to watch for this object (keyed-views-plan.md 2.4); empty when the object has none."""
        record = self.companies.get(object_id) or self.themes.get(object_id) or {}
        return list(record.get('watch') or [])

    SCOPELESS = {'total_revenue', 'gross_margin', 'operating_margin', 'operating_expense_growth', 'total_expenses', 'operating_loss', 'tax_rate', 'capex'}

    def scope_and_source(self, object_id, measure, scope='', event_type='n/a'):
        """Use a reference name only on an exact match; preserve actual business qualifiers (D155)."""
        plain = re.sub(r'^(?:non[-_ ]?gaap|gaap)\s*', '', scope.strip(), flags=re.I)
        redundant = {'', measure.replace('_', ' ')}
        if measure in self.SCOPELESS and plain.casefold() in redundant:
            return '', 'none'
        for entry in self.watch_list(object_id):
            if (entry.get('measure') == measure and entry.get('scope')
                    and scope_key(entry['scope']) == scope_key(scope)
                    and (not entry.get('event_type') or entry['event_type'] == event_type)):
                return entry['scope'], 'watch'
        return scope, 'model'

    def fiscal_year_end_month(self, object_id):
        """12 for a theme, a company whose fiscal year is the calendar year, or an unknown object."""
        company = self.companies.get(object_id)
        return int((company or {}).get('fiscal_year_end_month') or 12)

    def fiscal_period(self, object_id, year, bare_is_calendar=False):
        """Convert an entire single-year name. Explicit calendar years stay calendar; other spans return None. A bare year
        (2026) is the company's fiscal year under the Chinese prompt versions (06-views: 公司的数按它的财年) and a calendar
        year under the English ones, whose request defines "FY2027, or 2026 for a calendar year"."""
        parsed = parse_year(year)
        if not parsed:
            return None
        kind, y = parsed
        month = 12 if kind == 'calendar' or (kind == 'bare' and bare_is_calendar) else self.fiscal_year_end_month(object_id)
        if month == 12:
            return f'{y}-01-01', f'{y}-12-31'
        start = f'{y - 1}-{month + 1:02d}-01'
        import calendar
        return start, f'{y}-{month:02d}-{calendar.monthrange(y, month)[1]:02d}'

    def canonical_year(self, object_id, year):
        """One spelling per year for the join between a view's year and a waiting dependency's year: a fiscal form
        (FY2027, fiscal year 2027, 2027财年) becomes FY2027 when the object's fiscal year differs from the calendar
        year, else 2027; a calendar form (calendar year 2026, CY2026, 2026自然年) becomes 2026; a bare year keeps its
        digits and is never reinterpreted as a fiscal year (an event dated "2026" means calendar 2026); text that is
        not one single year stays as written (a multi-year span never resolves a waiting dependency)."""
        parsed = parse_year(year)
        if not parsed:
            return (year or '').strip()
        kind, y = parsed
        if kind == 'fiscal' and self.fiscal_year_end_month(object_id) != 12:
            return f'FY{y}'
        return str(y)

    def fiscal_note(self, object_id, publication_day, english=False):
        """One line telling the model how this company's fiscal years map onto the calendar, so a number's year and
        due day are written right (NVDA's FY2027 ends in January 2027, not 2028)."""
        company = self.companies.get(object_id)
        if not company:
            return ''
        month = int(company.get('fiscal_year_end_month') or 12)
        year, pub_month = int(publication_day[:4]), int(publication_day[5:7])
        if month == 12:
            if english:
                return (f"{object_id}'s fiscal year is the calendar year and ends in December: this year is FY{year}, next year is FY{year + 1}; "
                        f'full-year figures are published in the annual report in January to March of the following year.')
            return f'{object_id} 的财年和自然年一样，12 月结束：今年是 FY{year}，明年是 FY{year + 1}；全年数在次年 1 到 3 月的年报里公布。'
        # the fiscal year is named by the calendar year in which it ends
        current = year if pub_month <= month else year + 1
        start_month = month % 12 + 1
        start_year = current - 1 if start_month > month else current
        report_month = month + 1 if month < 12 else 1
        if english:
            return (f"{object_id}'s fiscal year ends in month {month} and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY{current} runs from "
                    f'{start_year}-{start_month:02d} to {current}-{month:02d}; the publication day {publication_day} falls in FY{current}, so this year is FY{current} '
                    f"and next year is FY{current + 1}; FY{current}'s full-year figures are published in the annual report around {current}-{report_month:02d}; use that day as the due date.")
        return (f'{object_id} 的财年在 {month} 月结束，财年按结束的那一年命名：FY{current} 从 {start_year}-{start_month:02d} 到 {current}-{month:02d}，'
                f'发布日 {publication_day} 落在 FY{current}，所以今年是 FY{current}，明年是 FY{current + 1}；FY{current} 的全年数在 {current}-{report_month:02d} 前后的年报里公布，到期日按那天写。')


# The accepted spellings of one year (docs/research/2026-10-25-english/plan.md, "Period text"): a full match, nothing else.
FISCAL_YEAR = re.compile(r'(?:FY\s*|fiscal\s+(?:year\s+)?)(\d{4})|(\d{4})\s*财年|FY\s*(\d{2})', re.I)
CALENDAR_YEAR = re.compile(r'(?:CY\s*|calendar\s+(?:year\s+)?)(\d{4})|(\d{4})\s*自然年|(\d{4})\s*calendar\s+year', re.I)
BARE_YEAR = re.compile(r'(\d{4})\s*年?')


def parse_year(text):
    """('fiscal' | 'calendar' | 'bare', year) for text that names exactly one year, else None. A bare year takes the
    object's fiscal year when its period is computed (06-views: 公司的数按它的财年)."""
    value = (text or '').strip()
    if not value:
        return None
    m = FISCAL_YEAR.fullmatch(value)
    if m:
        year = m.group(1) or m.group(2) or m.group(3)
        return 'fiscal', int(year) if len(year) == 4 else 2000 + int(year)
    m = CALENDAR_YEAR.fullmatch(value)
    if m:
        return 'calendar', int(m.group(1) or m.group(2) or m.group(3))
    m = BARE_YEAR.fullmatch(value)
    if m:
        return 'bare', int(m.group(1))
    return None


def scope_key(scope):
    """A scope name as compared: case, spacing, dashes and the words revenue/segment do not distinguish two scopes."""
    s = re.sub(r'[\u2013\u2014]', '-', (scope or '')).replace('＋', '+').replace('&amp;', '&')
    s = re.sub(r'\b(revenue|segment|business|division)\b', '', s, flags=re.I)
    return re.sub(r'\s+', ' ', s).strip().casefold()


def load(path):
    with open(path, encoding='utf-8') as handle:
        return Universe(json.load(handle))
